[33mPat Connaughton led the bench with 14 points, seven rebounds, four assists, two steals and two blocks. Both teams return[0m
[33mto action on Thursday, with Milwaukee playing host to the Los Angeles Clippers and Houston welcoming the Denver Nuggets [0m
[33mto Toyota Center.": "94",[0m                                                                                               
[33m          "The Chicago Bulls defeated the Orlando Magic, 90 - 80, at United Center on Friday evening. The Bulls (8 - 25)[0m
[33measily overcame a slim one - point first - quarter deficit in the second period and took a 46 - 39 lead into [0m           
[33mintermission. Chicago's stifling defense didn't have much trouble with the Magic (14 - 17), which only shot 33 percent, [0m
[33mincluding 24 percent from three - point range. The home squad particularly clamped down over the final 12 minutes, [0m     
[33mholding Orlando to 17 points in the fourth quarter. The Magic were paced by Evan Fournier, who compiled 24 points, six [0m 
[33massists and three rebounds. Nikola Vucevic delivered a 19 - point, 19 - rebound double - double that also included four [0m
[33massists and four blocks. Aaron Gordon produced 14 points, 12 rebounds and four assists. D.J. Augustin mustered eight [0m   
[33mpoints, three rebounds and two assists. The Bulls were led by Lauri Markkanen, who racked up 32 points, six rebounds, [0m  
[33mthree asists and one block. Robin Lopez followed with a bench - leading 14 points and also had four rebounds, two [0m      
[33massists and one block. Kris Dunn filled out the stat sheet with 12 points, eight rebounds, seven assists and two steals.[0m
[33mJustin Holiday posted an 11 - point, 10 - rebound double - double that also included one assist, one steal and one [0m     
[33mblock. The Magic heads back home to face the Miami Heat on Sunday evening, while the Bulls pay a visit to the Cleveland [0m
[33mCavaliers on Sunday evening as well.": "80",[0m                                                                            
[33m          "The Washington Wizards defeated the host Chicago Bulls, 134 - 125, at Capital One Arena on Saturday. These [0m  
[33mteams made a huge move at the trade deadline on Thursday, as many of those pieces were huge factors here. Washington got[0m
[33mthe better of Chicago thanks to a 42 - 29 second quarter, as the Wizards led by at least six points for the entirety of [0m
[33mthe second half. The Wizards offense was unstoppable, as they shot 58 percent from the field and 44 percent from three -[0m
[33mpoint range while holding Chicago to 50 percent from the field and 25 percent from long range. Much of that can be [0m     
[33mattributed to ball movement, with the Wizards out - assisting the Bulls, 38 - 28. Bench production was also critical, [0m  
[33mwith Washington outscoring Chicago's bench, 64 - 38. The Wizards (24 - 32) were led by Bradley Beal, as he tallied 31 [0m  
[33mpoints, two rebounds, four assists and four steals. Trevor Ariza accumulated 19 points, four rebounds and four assists. [0m
[33mTomas Satoransky finished with seven points, seven rebounds and 11 assists. Jabari Parker led the bench with 20 points, [0m
[33mfive rebounds and six assists. Bobby Portis also played well off the bench, amassing 10 points, 12 rebounds and four [0m   
[33massists. The Bulls (13 - 43) were led by Zach LaVine, as he accrued 26 points, four rebounds and six assists. Lauri [0m    
[33mMarkkanen finished with 20 points, 11 rebounds and four assists. Otto Porter generated 17 points, two rebounds, two [0m    
[33massists and two steals while Robin Lopez totaled 18 points, three rebounds and two blocks. Wayne Selden Jr. led the [0m    
[33mbench with 17 points and four boards. Both teams return to action on Monday, with Chicago playing host to the surging [0m  
[33mMilwaukee Bucks and Washington traveling to face the Detroit Pistons.": "125",[0m                                          
[33m          "The Boston Celtics defeated the New Orleans Pelicans, 113 - 100, at TD Garden on Monday night. The Celtics [0m  
[33m(16 - 10) came into the game fielding something akin to a preseason roster, considering Kyrie Irving (shoulder), Al [0m    
[33mHorford (knee) and Gordon Hayward (illness) were all out of action. They let their deep roster do what it's intended to [0m
[33mdo, however, jumping out a 28 - 21 first - quarter lead and remaining consistent throughout all four quarters. Boston [0m  
[33mheld off any designs of a Pelicans (14 - 15) comeback in the final 12 minutes by outscoring their visitors, 30 - 28. New[0m
[33mOrleans suffered a key injury during the game, as Nikola Mirotic exited the contest with an ankle injury after logging [0m 
[33mjust seven minutes. Anthony Davis led the Pelicans with 41 points, a total he supplemented with seven rebounds, two [0m    
[33massists and four steals. Julius Randle provided 20 points as the only other double - digit scorer on New Orleans. Tim [0m  
[33mFrazier mustered eight points and dished out 10 assists. Jrue Holiday could only compile seven points on 3 - for - 10 [0m  
[33mshooting. He added six assists, one rebound and three steals. Marcus Morris paced the Celtics with 31 points, adding [0m   
[33mfour rebounds and four assists. Jayson Tatum registered 21 points, six boards, one assist and one block. Jaylen Brown [0m  
[33mpoured in 19 points and also supplied seven rebounds, three assists and one block. Semi Ojeyele totaled 11 points and [0m  
[33msix rebounds. Terry Rozier filled in for Irving and collected 10 points, seven rebounds, six assists and two steals. The[0m
[33mPelicans head back home to take on the Oklahoma City Thunder on Wednesday night, while the Celtics hit the road and take[0m
[33mon the Washington Wizards on Wednesday evening as well.": "100",[0m                                                        
[33m          "The Portland Trail Blazers defeated the Los Angeles Clippers, 131 - 127, at Staples Center on Monday evening.[0m
[33mMonday's contest saw two of the premier teams in the Western Conference go head - to - head, and the game did not [0m      
[33mdisappoint. Portland (17 - 13) squeaked by LA (17 - 13) in the game's final minute thanks to clutch play from its stars.[0m
[33mWhile the Trail Blazers had led by double - digits in the fourth quarter, the Clippers quickly caught up in the final [0m  
[33mfive minutes of action. LA took a bit of a blow after big man Montrezl Harrell was assessed a flagrant foul and ejected [0m
[33mfor elbowing Portland's Jusuf Nurkic with just over seven minutes left in the fourth quarter. Still, the Clippers fought[0m
[33mback, carried by a career night from star forward Tobias Harris. Harris led his team with 39 points, a new career high. [0m
[33mPortland, however, answered back, as Damian Lillard hit a handful of clutch shots down the stretch and scored 39 points [0m
[33mof his own. It was C.J. McCollum, though, that hit the dagger for the Blazers, knocking down a step - back jumper to [0m   
[33mmake it a two - possession game with 27 seconds remaining. Lillard shot 11 - of - 20 from the field, including 6 - of - [0m
[33m7 from three - point range, en route to his big night. 21 of Lillard's points came in the third quarter, as he simply [0m  
[33mcould not miss in the second half. McCollum, meanwhile, added another 27 points in the win. Nurkic scored 20 as well, [0m  
[33madding seven rebounds and two blocks. Harris's 39 points led all Clippers scorers and set a new career - high for the [0m  
[33mbudding star. He added 11 rebounds on the night. The Clippers, who remain without star guard Lou Williams (hamstring), [0m 
[33msaw 24 points from rookie point guard Shai Gilgeous-Alexander. Harrell had 15 points as well prior to his ejection. [0m    
[33mPortland will host the Memphis Grizzlies on Wednesday, while LA will see the Dallas Mavericks on Thursday evening.": [0m   
[33m"127",[0m                                                                                                                  
[33m          "The Atlanta Hawks took down the Los Angeles Clippers, 123 - 118, at Staples Center on Monday evening. Hawks [0m 
[33mpoint guard Trae Young set the bar high the last time these two teams met, delivering a season - high 17 assists against[0m
[33mthe Clippers in November. On Monday, he once again left an impression on LA, scoring a team - high 26 points to help his[0m
[33mteam earn a much - needed win. The Hawks (16 - 33) went up early thanks to strong play from Young and John Collins, who [0m
[33mscored seven points each in the first quarter. While LA (27 - 23) fought its way back and evened the game at 71 - 71, a [0m
[33mlate third - quarter run helped Atlanta maintain control of the game. Big man Alex Len helped spark the run by scoring [0m 
[33meight points in under three minutes of action. The win brought Atlanta to 3 - 3 in its last six games, as the team [0m     
[33mcontinues to distance itself from its slow start to the season. Young has been a big part of that, averaging 18 points [0m 
[33mper game since the start of January. In addition to his strong scoring on Monday, he dished out eight assists and [0m      
[33mcommitted only one turnover. Collins finished the game with 22 points, while Len contributed another 19 off the bench. [0m 
[33mAs a team, Atlanta shot over 50 percent from the field. Los Angeles, meanwhile, was led by 30 points from star forward [0m 
[33mTobias Harris. Harris also flirted with a triple - double, grabbing eight boards and dishing out seven assists. Off the [0m
[33mbench, Lou Williams and Montrezl Harrell combined for 39 points and five steals, with Williams also recording nine [0m     
[33massists. However, the team could not quite match Atlanta's efficient production, shooting 48 percent from the field. The[0m
[33mloss snapped a three - game winning streak for the Clippers. Next on the agenda for Atlanta is a trip to Sacramento on [0m 
[33mWednesday. The Clippers, meanwhile, will shift their focus to their tilt with their crosstown rival, the Lakers, on [0m    
[33mThursday.": "118",[0m                                                                                                      
[33m          "The Memphis Grizzlies defeated the visiting Los Angeles Clippers, at FedEx Forum on Wednesday evening. The [0m  
[33mGrizzlies got out to a great start at home, as they outscored the visitors, 27 - 15, through the first quarter. The [0m    
[33mGrizz kept the heat on in the second, where they pushed their lead to 16 at the halfway point, however, the Clippers did[0m
[33mnot back down, and managed to cut the deficit to nine points by halftime. The Clippers carried the energy into the third[0m
[33mand used an 110 run to take a one - point lead with 7:50 left in the quarter. The Grizzlies held their ground from [0m     
[33mthere, as the teams went into the fourth tied at 69. The Grizzlies took an edge early in the fourth and slowly built a [0m 
[33mnine - point lead, with seven minutes left in the contest. They held strong from there, to earn their eighth home win. [0m 
[33mMike Conley led the Grizzlies with 22 points, seven rebounds, four assists, two steals and two blocks, in 34 minutes. [0m  
[33mJaMychal Green followed up with 19 points, 11 rebounds, two steals and one assist, in 28 minutes off the bench. Jaren [0m  
[33mJackson Jr. added 13 points, six rebounds and one block. The Grizzlies shot 44 percent from the field, including 7 - of [0m
[33m- 28 from long range. Meanwhile, Boban Marjanovic led the Clippers with 19 points, eight rebounds, one assist and one [0m  
[33msteal, in 13 minutes off the bench. Danilo Gallinari followed up with 17 points, five rebounds, two assists and one [0m    
[33msteal, in 33 minutes. Lou Williams added 12 point and seven assists, in 25 minutes off the bench. The Clippers (16 - 8) [0m
[33mwill look to bounce back as they play host to the Heat on Saturday. The Grizzlies (14 - 9) take on the Pelicans in New [0m 
[33mOrleans on Friday.": "69"[0m                                                                                               
