[33mdid not look back from there, as they pushed the lead to nine before settling on a 30 - 25 lead heading into the second.[0m
[33mThey kept their foot on the gas and quickly pushed their lead to 11, and although the Pacers made a push, the Bucks [0m    
[33mmaintained their cushion and took a 62 - 53 lead into halftime. The third quarter once again belonged to Milwaukee, as [0m 
[33mthe Buck outscored the Pacers 31 - 23 in the quarter, to take a 93 - 76 lead into the final frame. The Pacers battled [0m  
[33mhard but the Bucks matched them point for point in the fourth, to walk away with their second straight win. Giannis [0m    
[33mAntetokounmpo led the way for Milwaukee, with 26 points, 15 rebounds, five assists, two steals and one block, in 31 [0m    
[33mminutes. Khris Middleton followed up with 23 points, four rebounds, four assists and one steal, while Malcolm Brogdon [0m  
[33mtallied 15 points, seven assists, four rebounds and two steals. The Bucks shot 47 percent from the field, including 17 -[0m
[33mof - 47 from long range. Meanwhile, Victor Oladipo led the Pacers with 25 points, five rebounds, one assist and one [0m    
[33mblock, in 31 minutes. Doug McDermott chipped in 14 points on 5 - of - 8 shooting, in 20 minutes off the bench, while [0m   
