[33m          "Joel Embiid_('The Philadelphia 76ers defeated the visiting Memphis Grizzlies, 103 - 95, at Wells Fargo Center[0m
[33mon Sunday evening. The Sixers got out to a quick, 10 - 3, lead but the Grizzlies stuck with it, leading to a, 26 - 25, [0m 
[33madvantage for the home team, after one quarter. The 76ers stayed on top in the second, where they outscored the [0m        
[33mGrizzlies, 28 - 19, to take a, 54 - 44, lead by halftime. Things tightened up again in the second half, as both teams [0m  
[33mmatched each other for 24 points in the third quarter, leaving the Sixers ahead by 10 heading into the fourth. The [0m     
[33mGrizzlies started the fourth quarter with a quick 9 - 1 run, to make it a two - point game. However, the 76ers answered [0m
[33mright back, pushing their lead back to nine, with five minutes left. The Grizzlies cut it as close as a four - point [0m   
[33mdeficit, but could not do better than that, as the 76ers held on to earn their fourth straight win. J.J. Redick led [0m    
[33mPhilly with 24 points on 9 - of - 17 shooting, in 30 minutes. Jimmy Butler tallied 21 points, three rebounds, two [0m      
[33massists and a block. Ben Simmons finished with 19 points, 12 rebounds, six assists and two steals, while Joel Embiid [0m   
